#
# t3g = t3f + v52h WORKER-side authoritative boundary clamp (1 file changed):
#   - gpu_model_runner: execute_model trims spec-decode row counts with a
#     worst-case-safe mamba block-boundary rule BEFORE the input gather:
#     (1) if [est - (prev_sched_rows-1), est] straddles a 2048 boundary ->
#         degrade the step to 1 row (no drafts); (2) else if est%bs + rows
#         > bs -> clamp to room. Root fix v2 for crash-4 R1: t3f proved the
#     scheduler-side v52g clamp insufficient in async mode (DEF-PP
#     snapshots: 8-row steps EXECUTED at actual 2046/2044 while clamps
#     engaged on estimates; async shortfall = prev placeholder optimism -
#     acceptance, up to prev rows-1). The worker trim rides the natural
#     shortfall correction machinery downstream. Scheduler v52g clamp
#     stays as belt-and-braces.
# All other overlays identical to t3f (md5-gated).
